*.pyc
np_dump
.coverage
.lock
bench/wl_up/*.json
bench/wl_up/reachability.csv
bench/wl_up/rulesets/*-ruleset
bench/wl_ifi/*.json
bench/wl_i2/*.json
bench/wl_i2/reach.csv
bench/wl_i2/i2-json/*.json

bench/wl_stanford/reach.csv
# Blanket, like every other workload above -- enumerating a single filename left
# the OTHER two generated artifacts (cchecks.json and the reachable.json ORACLE)
# visible as untracked, so running the integration tier dirtied the tree and a
# locally generated oracle was one `git add .` away from being committed. A
# single `*` does not cross `/`, so the tracked JSON under eval/ and
# stanford-json/ is unaffected.
bench/wl_stanford/*.json
bench/wl_stanford/stanford-json/*.json

bench/wl_ifi/convert.sh
bench/wl_ifi/*.css
bench/wl_ifi/*.html
bench/wl_ifi/*.orig.*
bench/wl_ifi/*.csv
# ...except the policy MATRICES, which are inputs, not artifacts: they are the
# tracked source `bench/reach_csv_to_checks.py` derives every wl_ifi check set
# from. `reachability.csv` predates the rule above and was tracked anyway;
# stating both exemptions keeps that intentional rather than historical.
!bench/wl_ifi/reachability.csv
!bench/wl_ifi/reachability_stateless.csv

bench/wl_example/reachability.csv
bench/wl_example/policy.csv
bench/wl_example/*.json

bench/wl_tum/*.json
bench/wl_tum/rulesets/pgf.uni-potsdam.de-ruleset

bench/wl_generic_fw/*.json
bench/wl_generic_fw/*.csv

# Blanket like the workloads above, so a newly generated artifact cannot leak
# into a `git add .`. oracle.json is among them ON PURPOSE: it used to be
# hand-transcribed and tracked, and is now DERIVED from the vendored .smt2
# instances on every run (bench/wl_cloud/cloud_oracle.py). Tracking a generated
# oracle is how a benchmark ends up gated on an artifact nobody can rebuild --
# see CLOUD_BENCH_PLAN.md §1.8, and stanford-json/ for what that looks like
# years later. The raw scenario it is derived FROM is tracked instead, under
# bench/wl_cloud/cloud-tf/, with a SHA256SUMS the run verifies before deriving.
bench/wl_cloud/*.json


*.pdf
out
*.svg

# The vendored raw scenario is tracked WHOLE, exactly as the dataset ships it,
# so no curation decision of ours sits between the archive and the benchmark.
# network.svg is a rendering nothing reads, but `*.svg` above would drop it
# from a fresh clone and SHA256SUMS -- which covers the whole directory --
# would then fail to verify. Placed BELOW the rule it exempts from, because
# the last matching pattern is the one that decides.
!bench/wl_cloud/cloud-tf/network.svg

*.so
*.so.bak

examples/example-ruleset

*.swp

report.md
